Philip Henry Wicksteed born 1844, was an English scholar and Unitarian theologian known for his contributions to classics, medieval studies and economics. 
He was also a Georgist and literary critic. 

Born the son of a clergyman he was exposed to Nonconformist views from his family world view. 
Wicksteed was educated at University College London, the seminary foor nonconformist ministers. 
Unitarian ministry with is father shaped his world view greatly. 
The book Progress and Poverty is one of his best known works. 
